SPEC — Automatic Repository Attachment for VS Code
Status: proposed
Scope: VS Code extension + CLI workspace resolver
Goal: start/resume governed work without manually opening a repository first
1. Problem
Today, Singularity Flow relies on the repository currently open in VS Code to:
locate singularity/workflow.yml;
run the CLI with the correct working directory;
determine the Git branch and Work ID;
expose source files to Copilot.
This creates a confusing dependency:
Select Singularity workspace
→ manually find and open repository
→ possibly open another VS Code window
→ attach Story session
→ start Copilot
The selected Singularity workspace already knows its repositories. Requiring the user to locate one again is unnecessary.
2. Desired behavior
The user should be able to start from the Singularity Flow sidebar:
Select workspace
→ select or start Story
→ Singularity resolves repository
→ clone/fetch working copy if necessary
→ attach it to the current VS Code window
→ attach Story session
→ open governed Copilot handoff
No manual repository opening and no additional VS Code window.
3. Terminology
Singularity workspace: project scope containing repository and capability mappings.
Delivery repository: repository where a Story is implemented.
Working copy: local clone or Git worktree used for one Story.
Attach repository: add the working-copy directory to the current VS Code window.
Attach session: select a Work ID, branch, phase, and governed agent for CLI and Copilot operations.
Repository attachment and session attachment are separate operations.
4. User experience
4.1 Selecting a workspace
Selecting a workspace must immediately load:
workspace identity;
declared repositories;
capabilities;
active and completed Stories;
Lifecycle, Inbox, Configuration, and Logs.
It must not require an open repository.
4.2 Starting a Story
The Story intake form determines the delivery repository using this precedence:
Repository explicitly selected by the user.
Repository mapped to the selected delivery capability.
Only eligible delivery repository in the workspace.
Otherwise, display a repository picker.
If no repository can be resolved, show:
Select the repository where this Story will be delivered.

Do not show “Open a repository first.”
4.3 Resuming a Story
For an existing Story, use its pinned repository ID. The user must not be asked to select it again.
Show a preview:
Story             WRK-123
Repository        mobile-app
Branch            WRK-123
Local directory   /workspaces/payments/worktrees/mobile-app/WRK-123
Remote status     Up to date
Current phase     implementation
Agent             developer
Primary action:
Continue in this window

4.4 Repository attachment
After confirmation, the extension:
Resolves or materializes the working copy.
Fetches the required remote references.
Checks out the exact Story branch.
Attaches the Story session.
Adds the directory using vscode.workspace.updateWorkspaceFolders().
Refreshes the Singularity views.
Offers to open Copilot Chat with the governed handoff.
The extension must not call APIs that open a separate VS Code window.
4.5 Copilot handoff
After attachment, show:
WRK-123 is ready in mobile-app. Phase: implementation. Agent: developer.

Actions:
Continue with Copilot
Open Story dashboard
Open terminal in Story
Not now
The governed handoff must include:
workspace ID;
repository ID and absolute working directory;
Work ID and branch;
workflow and current phase;
governed agent;
approved prior-phase artifacts;
active evidence;
applicable world-model context;
deterministic next action.
5. Working-copy strategy
Do not switch branches underneath another active Story.
Use this policy:
Situation	Behavior
Repository is absent locally	Clone into the workspace repository area
Repository is present and unused	Use the existing clone
Correct Story branch is already checked out	Reuse it
Another branch has uncommitted changes	Create a dedicated Git worktree
Another Story uses the repository	Create a dedicated Git worktree
Remote Story branch exists	Fetch and create a tracking worktree
Story branch does not exist	Create it only as part of confirmed Story start
Path is outside the selected workspace	Reject unless explicitly imported


Recommended layout:
<workspace>/
  repos/
    mobile-app/
  worktrees/
    mobile-app/
      WRK-123/
      WRK-456/
The layout is local infrastructure and must not be committed.
6. CLI interfaces
Add:
singularity-flow workspace repository resolve \
  --workspace <WORKSPACE-ID> \
  --work-id <WORK-ID> \
  --json
Read-only. Returns repository, clone, branch, and attachment status.
singularity-flow workspace repository materialize \
  --workspace <WORKSPACE-ID> \
  --work-id <WORK-ID> \
  [--repository <REPOSITORY-ID>] \
  [--fetch] \
  --json
Creates or repairs the working copy but does not open VS Code.
singularity-flow workspace session attach \
  --workspace <WORKSPACE-ID> \
  --work-id <WORK-ID> \
  [--repository <REPOSITORY-ID>] \
  [--agent <AGENT-ID>] \
  --json
Attaches the local Flow session in the resolved working copy.
Short Copilot commands:
/sf-workspace <WORKSPACE-ID>
/sf-session <WORK-ID>
/sf-resume <WORK-ID>
/sf-session must resolve the repository from the workspace instead of inspecting arbitrary repositories on the machine.
