10. State and authority
Information	Authority
Workspace registry	Existing machine-local workspace registry
Repository definitions	Workspace/capability configuration
Work ID and repository mapping	Governed Story state
Branch and remote receipt	Governed Story state
Local clone/worktree path	Machine-local workspace metadata
Active agent and session	.git/singularity-flow/session.json in the working copy
Folders attached to VS Code	VS Code window state
Lifecycle progress	Governed Story branch/state


VS Code folder attachment must never become lifecycle authority.
11. Safety rules
Never scan the machine for matching repositories.
Inspect only repositories declared by the selected workspace.
Never force-push.
Never discard local changes.
Never switch a dirty repository to another Story branch.
Never infer the target repository from a similarly named folder.
Never create a branch until Story intake is confirmed.
Never open another VS Code window automatically.
If workspace trust is required, stop and let VS Code display its native trust prompt.
Treat SSH, proxy, certificate, and credential failures as actionable errors without partially attaching a session.
12. Error handling
Replace generic messages with specific recovery actions.
Missing clone
mobile-app is not available locally. Clone it into this workspace?

Dirty working copy
The existing mobile-app clone has uncommitted changes. Singularity can create an isolated worktree for WRK-123 without disturbing them.

Missing remote branch
No remote branch exists for WRK-123. Resume cannot continue. Start the Story or verify its branch receipt.

Access failure
Singularity could not fetch mobile-app. Check Git authentication, corporate proxy, or certificate settings, then retry.

Ambiguous repository
This Story is eligible for multiple repositories. Select where it will be delivered.

13. Refresh behavior
After attachment or session changes:
Invalidate the workspace snapshot cache.
Refresh Workspaces, Lifecycle, Inbox, Configuration, and Logs.
Start file watchers for the attached working copy.
Ignore temporary lock and telemetry writes that do not change lifecycle state.
Retry a drifting snapshot with bounded backoff before displaying an error.
14. Test plan
Repository resolution
One repository defaults automatically.
Capability mapping selects the correct repository.
Multiple eligible repositories produce a picker.
Existing Story uses its pinned repository.
Undeclared repositories are rejected.
Materialization
Missing repository is cloned.
Existing clean clone is reused.
Dirty clone creates an isolated worktree.
Existing remote Story branch is tracked.
A failed fetch leaves no false session attachment.
Concurrent Stories receive separate worktrees.
VS Code
Repository is added to the current window.
No command invokes vscode.openFolder with a new-window option.
Empty VS Code windows work.
Existing multi-root workspaces work.
Repeated attachment is idempotent.
Detachment removes only the workspace folder, not the files or Story session.
Lifecycle views refresh automatically.
Copilot
Handoff runs from the resolved repository.
Prompt contains the correct Work ID, repository, phase, and agent.
Approved artifacts and active evidence are included.
Copilot does not inspect the Singularity Flow product source by mistake.
Switching Stories changes context deterministically.
Safety
Dirty changes are preserved.
No force push occurs.
No arbitrary home-directory scanning occurs.
Branches are not created before confirmation.
Access failures do not leave partial Story state.
15. Acceptance criteria
The change is complete when:
A user can launch VS Code with no folder open.
Select a Singularity workspace.
Select an existing Story or complete Story intake.
Continue in the current window.
Have the correct repository cloned or worktree materialized.
See it added to the same VS Code window.
Open Copilot with the correct governed Story context.
Run /sf-status and receive status for that Story—not for the Singularity Flow product repository.
Complete this without manually browsing to or opening a repository folder.
